nce they are at an end and immediately left of the teal house (28, 31). Thus teal and Michelle are at **2** (42). Violet is at **1** (17). Gold must be at **8**, with Sapphires at **7** (13, 19).\n\n2. **Fix positions 7 and 8.** Gucci must be at **8**, because Michael Kors is immediately to its left (2, 11). Consequently Pearls, Ducati, and swimming are at **8** (40, 49, 4). Scuba diving is therefore at **7**, so Wang and the Atlanta Falcons are at **7** (21, 22, 38). Mohsen must be at **8**, being to the right of the Falcons (27).\n\n3. **Fix positions 1–3.** History is at **1**, since it is at an end and immediately left of the Ravens (14, 47). Hence the Ravens are at **2**, and grey, Obsidians, and the Miami Dolphins are at **3** (25, 41, 36).\n\n4. **Locate Mandy and the Chiefs.** Let \\(k\\) be the Chiefs’ position. Benelli, base jumping, and science fiction are also at \\(k\\), with Emeralds at \\(k+1\\) (1, 45, 46, 29). Clue 24 gives\n   \\[\n   3<\\operatorname{pos}(\\text{Mandy})<k,\n   \\]\n   so \\(k\\ge5\\). Position 7 belongs to the Falcons, position 8 cannot have Emeralds immediately after it, and \\(k=6\\) would put Emeralds at 7, where Sapphires already are. Thus **\\(k=5\\)**, Emeralds are at **6**, and Mandy is at **4**.\n\n5. **Finish the names.** Corals must precede Benelli at 5 (26). They cannot occupy 1 or 3 because those gemstones are fixed, nor 2 because Corals require the magenta house (16), while 2 is teal. Hence magenta is at **4**. Pink must precede Emeralds at 6 (39), so pink is at **5**. Turquoise can now only be at 6 or 7; it cannot be at 7 because Moonstones would then occupy 6, already Emeralds (3). Therefore turquoise, running, and Ali are at **6** (9, 18, 20).\n\n   Jones is at **1**: he is at an end, and 8 is Mohsen (34). The only unassigned name positions are now **3 and 5**, for Mallika and Rajiv. The remaining team positions are **4 and 8**, for the Cardinals and Rams. Because the Cardinals must be left of Rajiv (33), they must